# 92. Page, Workspace and Navigation Context

Because the ACCP may appear beside every TitanGold screen, Artemis may use
current product context to reduce unnecessary clarification.

Page context is convenience, not authorization.

## 92.1 Canonical Page Context

Where applicable, the ACCP may receive a bounded canonical context such as:

- Current route
- Product module
- Selected Agent
- Selected provider
- Selected account
- Selected symbol
- Selected timeframe
- Selected portfolio
- Active filters
- Visible object ID
- Environment

Do not send the entire DOM or arbitrary page state when canonical context is
sufficient.

## 92.2 Context Visibility

When context materially affects interpretation, the UI should make the resolved
context visible to the user.

Examples:

`Portfolio · MEXC Spot · BTC/USDT`

or:

`Technical Agent · 4H`

This reduces hidden-context errors.

## 92.3 Stale Context

Page context must expire or be revalidated when:

- The user navigates
- The selected object changes
- The session resumes after a material delay
- The underlying object was deleted or replaced

Do not execute a sensitive action against stale UI context.

## 92.4 Navigation Capability

Artemis may navigate the user to a TitanGold surface through an explicit
navigation capability.

Navigation must be separate from mutation.

`Open the API settings`

may navigate without granting permission to change API settings.

## 92.5 Pronoun and Referential Resolution

Commands such as:

- `Analyze this`
- `Open the one that failed this morning`
- `Remove it`
- `Close that`

must resolve to one unambiguous canonical object before material mutation.

When resolution is ambiguous, Artemis must ask or present choices.

